# Issue #851: lowering: `.trim().to_string()` stays `ref String`, process::run rejects it as Vec[String] (NK1102)

[Open and answer this issue on GitHub](https://github.com/Nikaia-Foundation/Nikaia/issues/851).

`decision` · opened 2026-10-25 · updated 2026-10-29 · 1 comment

Part of #847 (found by step 2). Reproduced on 0.0.1222.

**Probe.**
```
use std::process
fn main() throws {
    let a = "  x ".trim().to_string()
    let o = process::run("echo", [a])
    println(o.stdout)
}
```
`nikaia run` gives `NK1102: process::run expects args to be Vec[String], but you're passing Vec[ref String]`. `.trim().clone()` is accepted.

